# Copy to PROJECT ROOT as .env.local (next to package.json). Do not put .env.local inside .next/ — Next.js will not load it.
#
# Local MongoDB (Compass + this app use the same URI):
#   1) Install the server: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/installation/
#      macOS (Homebrew): brew tap mongodb/brew && brew install mongodb-community && brew services start mongodb-community
#   2) If "connection refused" on port 27017, the mongod process is not running — start it first, then open Compass.
#   3) URI examples:
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://deni:<denideni>@cluster0.slofy.mongodb.net/

# Optional — database name (default: apex). Collections: newsletter_subscribers, contact_messages
# MONGODB_DB=apex
#
# Atlas: use mongodb+srv://... from the Atlas UI instead of localhost.
#
# Compass: New Connection → paste MONGODB_URI → connect → database "apex" appears after your first form submit.
# First newsletter signup creates a unique index on email (remove duplicate emails first if index creation errors).
